data: {"type":"agent_chunk","agent":"analyst","content":"- **Targeted cutting is the core mechanism:** A synthetic guide RNA directs Cas9 nuclease to a specific genome location, where DNA is cut [7]. The system is based on a simplified bacterial antiviral defense [7].\n\n- **Editing depends on cellular repair:** Gene knockouts break a target gene [2]. Supplying a repair template can replace a disease-causing mutation [2], and the cell's repair of the cut can incorporate an injected new gene [3].\n\n- **Applications are expanding:** CRISPR SWAPnDROP enables large-scale DNA transfer between bacterial species, demonstrated in *Escherichia coli* [4]."}

